Change the type of points used to draw the shapes.

By default the [`Braille`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Braille "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Braille") patterns are used as they provide a more fine grained result, but you might want to use the simple [`Dot`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Dot "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Dot") or [`Block`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Block "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Block") instead if the targeted terminal does not support those symbols.

The [`HalfBlock`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.HalfBlock "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::HalfBlock") marker is useful when you want to draw shapes with a higher resolution than with a grid of characters (e.g. with [`Block`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Block "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Block") or [`Dot`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Dot "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Dot")) but lower than with [`Braille`](../../symbols/enum.Marker.html#variant.Braille "variant ratatui::symbols::Marker::Braille"). This grid type supports a foreground and background color for each terminal cell. This allows for more flexibility than the `PatternGrid` which only supports a single foreground color for each 2x4 dots cell.

